  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Skies are clear across Nevada tonight \nas ridging begins to build over the state. This ridge will keep \nconditions dry and warm for several days, with temperatures \nclimbing to nearly ten degrees above normal by the weekend. A weak\nshortwave trough temporarily breaks the ridge Tuesday morning but\nit builds back quickly, keeping temperatures well above normal \nthrough Wednesday afternoon. Daytime highs continue to be in the \nlow 60s with overnight lows in the 30s. Winds remain light, with \nafternoon gusts still maxing out at 15 mph or less. The \natmospheric river event mentioned in yesterday\u2019s discussion \nremains surrounded by questions but is still on track to break the\nridge for the end of next week. This would decrease temperatures,\nwith highs in the 50s currently forecast for Friday. It could \nalso cause showers across the forecast area, although the strength\nof moisture with this system is still highly uncertain.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in a warming\ntrend and above normal temperatures this weekend and early next\nweek. Low confidence in impacts from the atmospheric river. No\nchanges from NBM output.",
